<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Russian judicial reform of 1864</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1864</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Judicial Reform of 1864</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Russian judicial reform of 1864 was one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-reforms-russia">Great Reforms</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-ii-of-russia">Alexander II</a>, which reorganised the courts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a>. It introduced public trials, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jury-trial">trial by jury</a> for serious criminal cases, independent judges, an organised legal profession and justices of the peace. The Russian Empire profile treats it as a significant step towards modern legal institutions within an autocratic state.</p></div>
